# Golem

Instance `res://addons/golem/scenes/player.tscn`.

Copy `addons/golem` into the game. Leave this repo's tests and its gdUnit4 behind. Replace that folder to update.

Tune the instanced player's exports, or drop a preset from `res://addons/golem/presets/` onto the Golem preset row in the inspector. A preset writes the whole configuration, including collision layers. The numbers are copied onto the instance.

The body starts on physics layer 1. The camera, the floor ray, the movement checks, and the ragdoll bones use physics layer 2 unless that instance or a preset sets them.

Name the node `Player` and attach `res://addons/golem/scripts/menu/golem_world.gd` only when the level should open the Escape menu.

The debug HUD stays in the player scene and starts hidden.

Action names, default keys, and the `toggle_mouse_mode` / `mouse_mode` split are in `addons/golem/docs/using-in-a-game.md`.
